/* ============================================================
   COURSE NAME - course extras

   OPTIONAL. Most courses need no assets/ folder at all.

   There is one design system and one copy of it: ../../assets/hub.css,
   which every page in the hub links first. This file is layered AFTER it
   and carries only rules that are genuinely unique to this course.

   Before you add anything here, ask two questions.

   1. Would a second course want this rule? Then it belongs in
      assets/hub.css, not here. The hub carried six byte-identical forks
      of an earlier design system, one of which had a rendering fix the
      other five never received, and de-forking them is why there is one
      copy now.
   2. Does it restyle a shared element? Grep every *.css in the repository
      for the selector first. The extras files already restyle .lab h4 and
      .stub-note h4, so a hub-side change to either lands differently here.

   This file does NOT carry the course's colour. A course's identity is a
   hue offset, declared as one line in the course-accent block of
   assets/hub.css:

       :root[data-course="COURSE-FOLDER-NAME"] { --course-hue: 0; }

   hub.js reads the course folder out of the URL and writes data-course on
   <html> before the first paint; hub.css rotates whichever of the six
   palettes the reader chose by that offset in OKLCH. A course with no line
   there wears the plain palette accent.

   Charts do not carry a course palette either. The semantic chart classes
   -- m-stat, s-signal, f-prob, t-alarm, sw-gold and the rest -- are a
   closed set shared by the whole hub and declared in hub.css. Never write
   a literal hex into a figure: it reads in one mode, vanishes in the
   other, and cannot follow the print stylesheet.
   ============================================================ */

/* Theme tokens are declared four times in hub.css: :root, the
   prefers-color-scheme: dark block, and the two explicit-choice selectors,
   because the appearance toggle must beat the OS. A token added to :root
   alone silently keeps its light value in dark mode, so any token declared
   here needs the same four homes, plus @media print if it paints anything.

   @media print cannot use a bare :root here either: the explicit-choice
   selector out-specifies it in every medium, which is why hub.css uses
   !important in its print block. */
